<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 2.0 pct in June - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 2.0 pct in June - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 2.90 billion zlotys, or two percent, in June to 151.16 billion after a 2.4 pct rise in May, preliminary central bank figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 11.3 percent in the January-June period against 12.0 percent in the same period of last year.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY			JUNE	MAY    JUNE '96</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		2.0	2.4	 1.4</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   151.16   148.26    116.91</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	26.39    25.75     21.53</p>
<p>  National currency		     124.77   122.52     95.38</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    26.84    25.93     22.35</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    94.31    91.67     64.16</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
